---
description: Pass event values as explicit callback arguments; do not use $event in templates
globs: "**/*.vue"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Event callbacks in templates

Pass the event value as an explicit argument.

When the handler already accepts that value, bind the function:

```vue
<SearchField @update:model-value="setQuery" />
```

When the call needs a wrapper, name the argument in the callback:

```vue
<ProductCard @select="(id) => emit('select', id)" />
```

```vue
<!-- ❌ $event -->
<ProductCard @select="emit('select', $event)" />
```

When an inline callback on a dynamic component would be implicitly `any`, declare a typed function and bind it:

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
function onSelect(id: string) {
  emit('select', id)
}
</script>

<template>
  <component :is="panel" @select="onSelect" />
</template>
```
